    "updated_at": "2026-11-26T17:29:39Z",
    "body": "The defect is still there in v0.27.0. That release contains the fix of PR #3060.\n\nPlease reopen this issue. Only a collaborator can reopen it.\n\nWhat I did:\n\n1. I downloaded the v0.27.0 release (Windows 11).\n2. Created facing operation. In Geometry tab I set it to Faces and selected box top surface. \n3. I turned the view to a low view angle.\n\nWhat I saw: the same defect as in the first report. The thick pick-outline highlight becomes a wedge that grows to the edge of the viewport.\n\nScreenshot (v0.27.0):\n\n<img width=\"1601\" height=\"954\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-11-26 192624\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c501dafe-f231-48fe-9cf1-27a8de93bab2\" />\n\n<img width=\"811\" height=\"508\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cf850372-bdde-46fc-bcd2-bcf4c67a003f\" \n/>\n\nAttached is project file as well.\n\n[box.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/35476172/box.zip)",
